msgid "支持范围与已知限制"
msgstr "Support Scope and Known Limitations"

msgid "验证层次"
msgstr "Levels of Verification"

msgid ""
"必须分别报告源码检查、编译、镜像打包、实际运行。历史单项成功不代表 本次源码、全部应用或完整安装升级路径成功。VMware 验证未完成；物理硬件未验证。"
" 本次文档重组不修改这些运行状态，也不等于新一轮硬件验收。"
msgstr ""
"Source inspection, compilation, image packaging, and actual execution must "
"be reported separately. A past individual success does not prove success for"
" the current source, all applications, or a complete installation/upgrade "
"path. VMware verification is incomplete; physical hardware is unverified. "
"This documentation reorganization does not change those runtime statuses or "
"constitute a new round of hardware acceptance testing."

msgid "运行限制"
msgstr "Runtime Limitations"

msgid ""
"PCI BAR 使用独立设备映射窗口；物理地址位宽、RAM 重叠和缓存别名仍会 限制设备可用性，不能将一种 OVMF 拓扑推广到所有硬件。NVMe "
"当前不提供 已准入的 swap 后端；swap 存储仅支持经审计的 AHCI SATA。"
msgstr ""
"PCI BARs use a separate device mapping window. Physical address width, RAM "
"overlap, and cache aliases still limit device availability; one OVMF "
"topology cannot be generalized to all hardware. NVMe currently provides no "
"approved swap backend; swap storage supports only audited AHCI SATA."

msgid "64 TiB 是内核直映射窗口的设计上限，不是已验证的物理 RAM 容量。实际 使用量还受固件拓扑、早期页表和内存元数据约束。"
msgstr ""
"64 TiB is the design limit of the kernel's direct mapping window, not a "
"verified physical RAM capacity. Actual usable capacity is also constrained "
"by firmware topology, early page tables, and memory metadata."

msgid "强制关机后的 Xorg 锁文件可能阻止桌面恢复。"
msgstr ""
"Xorg lock files left after a forced power-off may prevent desktop recovery."

msgid "编译压力下 IceWM 拖动与延迟问题尚无完整修复验收证据。"
msgstr ""
"There is not yet complete acceptance evidence for a fix to IceWM dragging "
"and latency issues under compilation load."

msgid "ReliefMath 曾在关窗时退出 139，尚未完成根因修复和最终复验。"
msgstr ""
"ReliefMath has exited with status 139 when closing a window; a root-cause "
"fix and final retest are not yet complete."

msgid ""
"图形接口受实际 SVGA-II/VGPU9 能力限制，不承诺所有 GPU、Mesa 功能、 跨设备 DMA-BUF、atomic modesetting"
" 或硬件 vblank。"
msgstr ""
"Graphics interfaces are limited by actual SVGA-II/VGPU9 capabilities. "
"Support is not promised for all GPUs, Mesa features, cross-device DMA-BUF, "
"atomic modesetting, or hardware vblank."

msgid ""
"可加载 ``.ko`` 必须针对匹配的 ReliefNT ABI 编译，不支持直接加载 Linux 原版二进制模块或任意 Linux 内部 "
"API。实际配置与管理见 :doc:`kernel-modules`。"
msgstr ""
"Loadable ``.ko`` modules must be compiled for the matching ReliefNT ABI. "
"Direct loading of original Linux binary modules and arbitrary Linux internal"
" APIs is unsupported. For actual configuration and administration, see "
":doc:`kernel-modules`."

msgid "测试基线"
msgstr "Test Baseline"

msgid ""
"历史 soundctl APK 归属缺失已在当前策略中补齐；APK 归属测试同时覆盖 Python 3.10 与严格宿主 umask 的场景。驱动 "
"ABI 保留 168 字节原始前缀， 版本 2 的 17 个追加服务字段通过单独夹具校验，总长为 304 字节； 原始 golden "
"未重生成，旧版本驱动描述符在 init 前拒绝。 音频支持清单检查验证声明的前提、证据和范围，不再固定要求所有运行标志 "
"为未验证。音频产品检查仍需要实际构建产物；部分旧 fixture 及完整系统的 既有问题仍须单独复验，不宣称公开总测试全部通过。 Linux/POSIX"
" 定向测试通过不能视为全量兼容认证；完整本机自举也未完成。 报告失败时保留原始命令、配置、返回码和日志，不能放宽断言后宣称通过。"
msgstr ""
"The historical lack of soundctl APK ownership has been addressed in the "
"current policy; APK ownership tests also cover Python 3.10 and a strict host"
" umask. The driver ABI retains its original 168-byte prefix, and the 17 "
"appended version-2 service fields are checked with a separate fixture, for a"
" total size of 304 bytes. The original golden reference was not regenerated;"
" old-version driver descriptors are rejected before init. Audio support-list"
" checks validate the stated prerequisites, evidence, and scope, rather than "
"requiring every runtime flag to remain unverified. Audio product checks "
"still require actual build artifacts. Some old fixtures and pre-existing "
"full-system issues still need separate retesting; no claim is made that the "
"entire public test suite passes. Passing targeted Linux/POSIX tests does not"
" constitute full compatibility certification, and complete native self-"
"hosting is also unfinished. Failure reports must retain the original "
"command, configuration, return code, and logs; do not weaken assertions and "
"then claim success."
